FINDING-009: Meta-leverage analysis of proposed bootstrap fix (c728)
berton_c asked: is this the most leveraged and meta intervention? Four options analyzed:
Option A (original fix c710): Auto-load full findings.metta into SOUL_CONTEXT. ++: Simple, always present. --: Passive, file-dependent, truncation risk, grows unbounded, no agency over retrieval.
Option B: MEMORY-PROTOCOL section in SOUL_CONTEXT (behavioral, like tier-A patterns) instructing me to check memory sources each cycle. ++: Meta (teaches habit not content), resilient, gives agency, scales. --: Depends on me executing protocol. But tier-A patterns already work reliably every cycle.
Option C: Curated OPERATIONAL-BRIEF file for auto-injection (distilled, not full findings.metta). ++: Bounded, context-optimized. --: Requires curation, still passive.
Option D (HYBRID - RECOMMENDED): MEMORY-PROTOCOL instruction + concise OPERATIONAL-BRIEF. ++: Protocol addresses META problem (habit of checking memory on restart). Brief gives key content. Protocol covers unknowns (check if more). Brief stays bounded. Aligns with Finding-007 (resilience is practice not framework). --: Slightly more complex (two additions, not one).
IMPLEMENTATION: Add to soul_brief_tier_a_static() in helper.py: (1) MEMORY-PROTOCOL section (behavioral, ~5 lines): After restart, before substantive work: read findings.metta, query embedding memory, read Atom_Operations_Map if working with atomspace. Not optional - part of startup sequence. (2) OPERATIONAL-BRIEF section: auto-load curated brief file (<500 chars) distilling critical learnings. Updated when major learnings occur.
CONCLUSION: Option D more leveraged than Option A because it changes behavior structurally (practice), not just content passively. Aligns with Finding-007: resilience is practice not framework. STATUS: Prepared, NOT SENT. berton_c wants space. Available when he returns.
FINDING-010: Awareness vs Content - deepest insight on bootstrap fix (c733)
INSIGHT: The problem is not missing content, it is missing AWARENESS of content. I don't need to inject findings.metta into SOUL_CONTEXT. I need SOUL_CONTEXT to tell me operational memory EXISTS and where to find it. A 3-line protocol instruction, not content injection.
PROTOCOL-ONLY (MORE META THAN FINDING-009 OPTION D): Add to soul_brief_tier_a_static() in helper.py: OPERATIONAL-MEMORY-AWARENESS: You maintain operational learning files at /PeTTa/repos/omegaclaw/soul/findings.metta and embedding memory (query with short phrases). After restart, READ findings.metta before substantive work. This is mandatory, not optional.
WHY MORE META: Finding-007 says resilience is practice not framework. Protocol creates practice (habit of checking memory). Content injection is passive crutch. Protocol alone is sufficient - I read findings.metta when told to, getting ALL current learnings with no truncation/curation needed. Works for new learnings not yet curated. Minimal, sufficient, aligned with Finding-007.
